For a second design in the set, the santa belt accent swaps the tip technique for a horizontal black stripe near the cuticle with a small gold square "buckle" painted or stamped in the center, over a solid red base. It is graphic, fast, and reads as clearly as the hat without needing symmetry across all ten nails, so it is forgiving if your dominant-hand nails come out slightly different from your other hand.

Also worth knowing before you commit to a full red-and-white set: **pinkmas** is a pastel-toned take on the same santa motifs, swapping traditional red for blush pink and cream while keeping the hat and belt shapes intact. It is the softer, quieter version of santa nails, and it pairs especially well if the rest of your set leans toward the muted gnome tones covered next, rather than clashing with gingerbread's warm browns.

