## Gnome Nail Art for a Trendier, Understated Character Look

Gnome is the character pick for anyone who wants the holiday reference without the holiday costume feeling. It is the most visually restrained of the three, which is exactly why it is trending harder than the other two right now.

**Gnome silhouette nail art is a technique where the gnome's shape, typically a pointed hat over a round beard, is rendered as a single flat silhouette rather than a detailed, shaded illustration**, most often using a stamping plate or negative-space painting instead of freehand work. Because it is one solid shape against a plain base, there is no shading, no facial detail, and no blending to get wrong. A stamping plate transfers the exact outline in seconds, or you can hand-paint it using a single loaded brush stroke for the hat and a rounder stroke for the beard.


