## How to Mix Gingerbread, Santa, and Gnome on One Set

**Yes, gnome and santa nails can be combined on one set, and gingerbread pairs into the same hand just as easily.** The technique that makes it work is treating each character as a separate finger, not a separate style layered onto every nail at once.

The cleanest split is one character per finger, repeated with a plain accent color filling in the remaining nails. A common version: gingerbread on the thumb and pinky, santa hat french tip on the index and ring, gnome silhouette as the standout middle-finger accent, with the rest of both hands in a single solid shade that ties the palette together, cream, sage, or soft red depending on which two characters you leaned toward.

